                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d910c6c-6292-31ed-a78a-0df3487b8548",
                        "entry_id": "4420a4c2-0182-35f7-bbdf-3afbc7b08e53",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Clumsy, awkward, maladroit, not dextrous, all thumbs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "29b5539e-eff7-4c93-89d7-93091b4cef24",
                                "sense_id": "9d910c6c-6292-31ed-a78a-0df3487b8548",
                                "text": "\"Well, I don't tease anybody but the men. I don't tease father or mother or you,—but men are fair game; they are such thumby, blundering creatures, and we can confuse them so.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "97033cf0-8a50-4a71-b8b3-491bb59744bb",
                                "sense_id": "9d910c6c-6292-31ed-a78a-0df3487b8548",
                                "text": "[…] he was propounding an improvement of Professor Armstrong's Heuristic method, whereby at the cost of three or four hundred pounds' worth of apparatus, a total neglect of all other studies and the undivided attention of a teacher of exceptional gifts, an average child might with a peculiar sort of thumby thoroughness learn in the course of ten or twelve years almost as much chemistry as one could get in one of those objectionable shilling text-books that were then so common…."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06b6871f-7cbf-4851-a4e4-51830eb30eb7",
                                "sense_id": "9d910c6c-6292-31ed-a78a-0df3487b8548",
                                "text": "The box was set down, the stiff buckles of its mildewed straps tackled by a dozen thumby hands, the lid hurled back."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e22bcd6f-e25d-42a6-bfa2-e1d7b2a03f62",
                                "sense_id": "9d910c6c-6292-31ed-a78a-0df3487b8548",
                                "text": "For as long as we have known him—and for most of us that has been for the lengths of our lifetimes—he has been the object of, and inspiration for, a delight so innocent and perfect that the attempt to analyse its sources seems an act of ingratitude, a laying on of thumby hands that will inevitably bollix the job."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6709dda5-be67-4784-9864-e7a431aa431a",
                                "sense_id": "9d910c6c-6292-31ed-a78a-0df3487b8548",
                                "text": "Some people are handy, but I am (no other word fits) thumby.\nThe handy learn to master each moder machine as soon as it hits the market. The thumby never graduate beyond the self-service island at the gas station."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac37cdb0-76e8-44e8-bded-52858062f504",
                                "sense_id": "9d910c6c-6292-31ed-a78a-0df3487b8548",
                                "text": "2015, Julie Lawson, A Ribbon of Shining Steel: The Railway Diary of Kate Cameron, Yale, British Columbia, 1882, Dear Canada series, Scholastic Canada, https://books.google.ca/books?id=h1X2CQAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false\nRachel was all thumbs when it came to embroidery, even thumbier than me."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f5f41f07-0b5a-3694-8388-9de91c936fdf",
                        "entry_id": "4420a4c2-0182-35f7-bbdf-3afbc7b08e53",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dirtied by thumb marks."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c74b1ecd-148d-4b4f-a9d9-02ef61c23b85",
                                "sense_id": "f5f41f07-0b5a-3694-8388-9de91c936fdf",
                                "text": "He would distinguish, too, between a library and a news-room, and would find no great attraction in the prospect of supplying the national youth with free but thumby copies of the sixpenny magazines."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
